{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The End of Heartache and Ascendancy feel like natural next choices because they combine aggressive riffs with melodic passages, matching what draws me to Colony, Soundtrack to Your Escape, and Figure Number Five.",
    "City of Evil and Mezmerize fit my interest in energetic heavy music with memorable melodies or varied rhythms, which connects with my recent choices of Ten Thousand Fists and 10.000 Days."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "St. Anger's raw, repetitive approach misses the balance of heaviness and melody I want right now, even though it shares the intensity of music in my history.",
    "Testify's rap-driven sound is less appealing to me now, while Fallen feels lighter than my preferred choices on this page. Being related to hard rock alone does not make either a strong next choice."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat heavy guitars and aggression as enough to connect my choices, although the way melody fits into that heaviness matters more to me.",
    "My past interest in different kinds of rock seems to be treated as equally relevant now, even though I currently favor the more melodic metal choices."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated interest in In Flames and Soilwork is a stronger clue than an isolated heavy album: I am drawn to aggressive playing that still has melodic hooks.",
    "I can find an album broadly appealing without choosing it now. Reise, Reise and See You On The Other Side interest me, but Ascendancy and The End of Heartache match my current preference more closely."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understand my interest in heavy music but sometimes miss that melody within the aggression is what makes an album my next choice."
}"}
